:name: U400 boot-to-running-RTOS (foundation for the §9b inject-and-run test)
:description: Boots the Aqara U400 Aliro firmware on the emulated EFR32MG24 (brd4186c) all the way to a RUNNING FreeRTOS -- app tasks created, scheduler context-switching -- by stubbing the three unmodeled boot-time hardware dependencies that otherwise hang the boot CPU BEFORE any application task is created. Leaves the machine booted and paused (no quit) so it can be `include`d by an experiment script that then injects/observes. See HANDOFF-NATIVE-DEBUG.md §9b.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FINDING (2026-07-23, this branch): the handoff §9b assumed "boot with the radio
# spin bypassed -> scheduler + tasks alive". That premise was WRONG as stated:
# the radio bring-up + I2C + filesystem mount all run on the boot path BEFORE the
# application task-creation function sub_8038d44, so under the plain RAIL bypass
# NO application task is ever created (verified: at the 0x803e736 stall, sub_8038d44
# has not run). Reaching task creation requires stubbing THREE unmodeled subsystems
# whose poll/assert loops hang the single boot thread:
#
#   1. Radio config-validator sub_80e3dce -> return 0 (success).
#      Without this: b . (infinite loop) at 0x803e736 (assert in sub_803e6d8,
#      cbz r0 -> nonzero return == failure). This is the wall the old bringup
#      scenario bottomed out at.
#   2. I2C transfer state-machine sub_803266c -> return 0 (transaction done).
#      Without this: spins in its own while(true) at 0x8032680.. polling the I2C
#      IF register (*(base+0x3c)) for flags 0x40/0x80/0x20 that never arrive
#      (no I2C slave modeled; base 0x5B000000 I2C0 / 0x50068000 I2C1).
#   3. Filesystem mount sub_804b8e0 -> return 1 (pretend already-mounted).
#      Without this: hangs in flash/littlefs reads (load_file_index retry-logging)
#      because the fs partition is not backed by the ELF image.
#
# WITH all three: boot reaches sub_8040e44 (app-main task) -> sub_8038d44 ->
# creates ALL worker tasks incl. pid_motor CONSUMER sub_80718FC (prio 0x1f) and
# producer sub_8072174. Verified the consumer RUNS then blocks on its mailbox,
# and the scheduler context-switches (PendSV @0x08006430 fires ~32/s). Silabs
# FreeRTOS uses a hardware timer (not ARM SysTick @0x080CEF48) for its tick.
#
# CAVEAT: one early task sub_80e2cb0 busy-spins (0x80e2d98<->0x80e2d9c, likely a
# companion-chip/peripheral wait); the scheduler still preempts it, so a post to
# the prio-31 consumer mailbox will still wake the consumer. This is EMULATION:
# no motor model, so "physical motion" remains unobservable -- the §9b test
# confirms the consumer AUTONOMOUSLY reaches the drive fn, nothing more.
#
# The RAIL-primitive knobs (sub_80e3d60 / sub_80e3e46.. family) are retained from
# the old bringup scenario; harmless, and keep the radio-config path quiet.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

$bin?=@/home/chen/aliro-renode/matter/aliro-u400/firmware/U400_primary_target.elf
$vtor?=0x08006000
include @scripts/silabs-vuln/boot_mg24.resc

# --- RAIL radio-config primitive knobs (return success) ---
sysbus WriteWord 0x80e3d60 0x2000
sysbus WriteWord 0x80e3d62 0x4770
sysbus WriteWord 0x80e3e46 0x2000
sysbus WriteWord 0x80e3e48 0x4770
sysbus WriteWord 0x80e3e56 0x2000
sysbus WriteWord 0x80e3e58 0x4770
sysbus WriteWord 0x80e3e86 0x2000
sysbus WriteWord 0x80e3e88 0x4770
sysbus WriteWord 0x80e3e96 0x2000
sysbus WriteWord 0x80e3e98 0x4770

# --- (1) radio config-validator sub_80e3dce -> return 0 ---
sysbus WriteWord 0x80e3dce 0x2000
sysbus WriteWord 0x80e3dd0 0x4770

# --- (2) I2C transfer state-machine sub_803266c -> return 0 ---
sysbus WriteWord 0x803266c 0x2000
sysbus WriteWord 0x803266e 0x4770

# --- (3) filesystem mount sub_804b8e0 -> return 1 (already mounted) ---
sysbus WriteWord 0x804b8e0 0x2001
sysbus WriteWord 0x804b8e2 0x4770

echo ">>> U400 booting to running RTOS (radio/I2C/fs stubbed) ..."
emulation RunFor "4.0"
echo ">>> Boot complete. PC (expect a running task, e.g. ~0x80e2d9x spin or elsewhere):"
sysbus.cpu PC
echo ">>> pid_motor consumer sub_80718FC is created and blocked on its mailbox; scheduler is live."
